  "worked_solution": "First, we use the definition of $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061A$ to rewrite the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}-\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061A} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}-{tan}^{2}\u2061A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}-\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061A}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}\u2061A}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity $1-{sin}^{2}\u2061A={cos}^{2}\u2061A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}\u2061A}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061A}-\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061A}=1\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
